        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stoneridge Investment Partners, LLC",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The text of section 10(b) as well as the rule 10b-5 promulgated by the Securities and Exchange Commission prohibit the use of any deceptive device by any person, indirectly or indirectly, in connection with the purchase or sale of a security. The various deceptive devices used by the Respondents in this case is conduct that is squarely covered by the text of the statute and by the rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Intended or known? I mean, I don't see -- what's in it for Scientific-Atlanta to defraud the shareholders? Is it enough that they just knew it would be used for that purpose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: In other words, it's deceptive but not deceptive in relation to, or for the purpose of, deceiving the -- someone like the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But don't aiders and abettors have to have that purpose as well? What distinguishes -- what distinguishes the liability that you propose from aider and abettor liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF STEPHEN M. SHAPIRO. ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS MR. SHAPIRO: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: My friend has just asked the Court to expand an implied cause of action by diluting traditional requirements such as the reliance requirement and by eroding this Court's precedent in the Central Bank case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Which I thought speak about aiders and abettors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you know, Mr. Shapiro, if in the law of torts and the restatement of torts or in other areas of the law there is some third classification that's between aider and abettor in principle?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAPIRO: I don't know the answer. Although in these statutes themselves there are such provisions not included in section 10(b). For example in section 18(a), if you cause some other person to make a false statement in a financial statement, you can be held liable, but they are not invoking it in section 18."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hungar",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF THOMAS G. HUNGAR ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hungar",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUNGAR: We haven't taken a position on that question, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number three, with respect to 20(e), how do my friends on the other side read 20(e) in connection with section 9 and section 18 of the Exchange Act, each of which provides remedies and private rights of actions against multiple parties?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-43",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1282ef6e108be025206d2793a2765e2cfbc5b85595a1dafe75db14563082f2fd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1282ef6e108b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Grossman. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
